tudents learn the language of uncertainty used throughout health statistics.", "children": [{"id": "97ba1253-5443-46d2-a168-fe60068f5acd", "type": "concept", "title": "Event"}, {"id": "af9e1f0d-c40a-46df-b483-dcce351c9d04", "type": "concept", "title": "Complement"}, {"id": "83a677e1-a306-417c-9777-5b6fe9c191a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Conditional probability"}, {"id": "9676013c-285e-412a-9887-b1f25f6d4c64", "type": "concept", "title": "Independence"}, {"id": "4110d712-8176-4e18-9e4c-a2c6f5e3fd9a", "type": "concept", "title": "Bayes intuition"}]}, {"id": "e3d5867f-543b-4135-98ce-2be541276ca0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Health Risks and Rates", "description": "This subtopic links probability to clinical and public-health measures.", "children": [{"id": "1d4ca4c4-b22a-4462-8474-382c3441e67a", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk"}, {"id": "56414a2a-ea6d-4cb5-a4b6-f2d18e6ddc3c", "type": "concept", "title": "Rate"}, {"id": "b197c013-9fb2-43b3-ac3b-b5132bb00a47", "type": "concept", "title": "Incidence"}, {"id": "134e8295-5a81-49a8-ba15-e6965fc1d7d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Prevalence"}, {"id": "628457f0-88d3-4559-98e7-4f722c6d3e41", "type": "concept", "title": "Cumulative incidence"}]}, {"id": "5d403d17-34b0-4628-afac-c464bbef0b61", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Diagnostic Test Reasoning", "description": "Students interpret tests using both accuracy and patient context.", "children": [{"id": "65e6e2b8-f4e7-4f48-bbdf-6ab61c33aeb6", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensitivity"}, {"id": "ad6b173c-5bdc-41c4-95db-ebfd675e512c", "type": "concept", "title": "Specificity"}, {"id": "9196e546-2556-4a22-9bd7-5e5265063898", "type": "concept", "title": "Positive predictive value"}, {"id": "2226e93a-a947-4b84-a508-8c64d5a5b607", "type": "concept", "title": "Negative predictive value"}, {"id": "5eb8bfe2-34a1-4b28-bf69-355ab1f00ae3", "type": "concept", "title": "Likelihood ratio"}]}]}, {"id": "16e5f16d-8301-4c3d-b402-9e3cd03b1524", "type": "topic", "title": "Probability Distributions Used in Health Research", "description": "Covers common distributions that model binary, count, continuous, and rare-event health outcomes.", "children": [{"id": "939f7e43-1307-4c02-b7d2-fd3156d19267", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Discrete Distributions", "description": "Students learn models for binary and count health outcomes.", "children": [{"id": "378a97ab-0e81-4130-9b12-7242f9afd466", "type": "concept", "title": "Bernoulli distribution"}, {"id": "d6807e31-550f-429a-b6a9-acb9435a391d", "type": "concept", "title": "Binomial distribution"}, {"id": "628a5dc5-179d-4930-b93f-d4fcc7d0a685", "type": "concept", "title": "Poisson distribution"}, {"id": "13d95af4-d4ff-4e7d-933d-95fdb7e818de", "type": "concept", "title": "Expected value"}, {"id": "797caf14-a66a-40da-a298-4f8394e842f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Variance"}]}, {"id": "f36c2a5c-bac4-4678-ba72-9d8d61ffb24d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Continuous Distributions", "description": "This subtopic covers common models for measurements like blood pressure or lab values.", "children": [{"id": "d216d457-b689-4523-b8cd-fe68cc083214", "type": "concept", "title": "Normal distribution"}, {"id": "32e27122-38fa-43df-86e7-4c8fa18e0821", "type": "concept", "title": "Standard normal"}, {"id": "b25becf4-7fc3-400b-aee6-dd7eccc69c29", "type": "concept", "title": "t distribution"}, {"id": "672a5c05-71f2-4dcb-a78f-037688458f40", "type": "concept", "title": "Skewness"}, {"id": "6c6ce151-c5d5-42c5-8b22-58aeb7cd8201", "type": "concept", "title": "Percentiles"}]}, {"id": "064c0f05-ab75-4dca-84fe-cc3bf36b8f56", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Distribution Choice", "description": "Students learn to match models to data and assumptions.", "children": [{"id": "9f024a3b-bd70-47bc-b2ed-2dc04e7c8979", "type": "concept", "title": "Outcome type"}, {"id": "3e041244-65f3-4b18-9b6c-58a1070f23f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Rare events"}, {"id": "3c2ba089-82f3-41e2-8c81-55d85fa885fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Overdispersion"}, {"id": "c0045667-cc6d-4081-9224-23734fa43b74", "type": "concept", "title": "Normal approximation"}, {"id": "a8b77c6b-ea88-4d89-b079-1cb884d917e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Empirical distribution"}]}]}, {"id": "0790e515-0281-489e-9654-e8bd296504ca", "type": "topic", "title": "Sampling, Study Design, Bias, Confounding, and the Central Limit Theorem", "description": "Explains how data are generated and why sampling design affects inference and validity.", "children": [{"id": "16b7702c-716b-4271-984c-93be9098d1e4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sampling and Representativeness", "description": "Students learn why who gets measured shapes what conclusions are valid.", "children": [{"id": "b7c29e78-f001-4f2c-83f0-65c364ac0c1b", "type": "concept", "title": "Target population"}, {"id": "6e19867f-55df-4f62-a345-100c226e4614", "type": "concept", "title": "Sample"}, {"id": "d0e772ce-c323-4b49-b2d7-7b4effe28fe6", "type": "concept", "title": "Sampling frame"}, {"id": "5630d22d-10db-4c9d-9c52-7a408c766291", "type": "concept", "title": "Selection bias"}, {"id": "e6ea9125-e62b-47f2-ba19-1231e22e2637", "type": "concept", "title": "Generalizability"}]}, {"id": "e41aa57d-e87c-4ace-9d80-fcde1a43f27d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Study Designs in Health Research", "description": "This subtopic connects statistics to the way health evidence is produced.", "children": [{"id": "5e088c3c-1410-416a-8e8d-d0ead3705b10", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-sectional study"}, {"id": "1da246fc-aced-43a6-aeff-2ad2bf43111b", "type": "concept", "title": "Cohort study"}, {"id": "84220ae5-a081-45d0-8dfa-7a9dee9c2aa0", "type": "concept", "title": "Case-control study"}, {"id": "0937b58a-2a7b-4cd0-8880-990d65bfd3c3", "type": "concept", "title": "Randomized controlled trial"}, {"id": "2731fa1f-a905-4cfc-bb1e-5e6a6af1bd99", "type": "concept", "title": "Ecological study"}]}, {"id": "07565af2-422d-4eef-afff-c99c5634811a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sampling Distributions and CLT", "description": "Students learn why estimates vary and why large samples support inference.", "children": [{"id": "ff8acfd3-a8c5-43a0-a40c-36fe5ffb0c28", "type": "concept", "title": "Sampling variability"}, {"id": "b4d16928-0ac5-47bc-9dc8-f1d84890911f", "type": "concept", "title": "Standard error"}, {"id": "4b8d0f4f-c5c7-4145-84e8-a9b0be721217", "type": "concept", "title": "Central limit theorem"}, {"id": "6e31b0a5-e3c3-4c9d-97f1-b215c6655adf", "type": "concept", "title": "Law of large numbers"}, {"id": "f6a7a302-88ef-4e90-9f1d-7d49eef3c145", "type": "concept", "title": "Margin of error"}]}]}, {"id": "3d12c0b4-4d11-438d-9839-81cde6213215", "type": "topic", "title": "Confidence Intervals, Estimation, Precision, and Clinical Interpretation", "description": "Shows how interval estimates communicate uncertainty around health effects and measures.", "children": [{"id": "a2604ae8-f02d-4f9d-ab41-35314c9857de", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Point and Interval Estimation", "description": "Students learn how estimates and uncertainty are reported.", "children": [{"id": "f4e66110-4538-4f3a-b30c-324a018f08b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Point estimate"}, {"id": "e894504c-4813-4607-9502-1c570e770ac3", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidence interval"}, {"id": "c304a5a1-43bb-4f27-99a8-df088ae3ec12", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidence level"}, {"id": "155dd243-c8ea-4cf6-a159-4dd878aec428", "type": "concept", "title": "Precision"}, {"id": "7645ce5f-cf6f-453c-80b0-da02f417086b", "type": "concept", "title": "Margin of error"}]}, {"id": "3a9e0fbd-e0b9-4b89-b5eb-0150acd27f7d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Intervals for Common Health Measures", "description": "This subtopic applies intervals to means, proportions, and effect measures.", "children": [{"id": "dbe56aa3-53eb-4643-8a85-ccae543b89de", "type": "concept", "title": "Mean difference CI"}, {"id": "cc611bcc-8976-492d-8aee-b777538bedc5", "type": "concept", "title": "Proportion CI"}, {"id": "f1a5fe5e-2372-43e9-9695-fdd76410ddf0", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk ratio CI"}, {"id": "7880dc36-e5b5-4cf9-8640-f9001e2cef45", "type": "concept", "title": "Odds ratio CI"}, {"id": "9a56877a-d3f8-4e42-a887-a75764ed577f", "type": "concept", "title": "Rate CI"}]}, {"id": "95a6b29a-e5d4-4d8d-876b-7906276a456a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Clinical Interpretation", "description": "Students learn to read intervals for decision relevance.", "children": [{"id": "8df767cf-717c-4d1f-96cf-6b7908966c35", "type": "concept", "title": "Null value"}, {"id": "65bf9bff-21d6-4017-8cbc-e23170915e3e", "type": "concept", "title": "Width of interval"}, {"id": "3da7a060-5763-47f4-9be2-456589e963d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Direction of effect"}, {"id": "e491f57b-b564-4331-9b7f-ec88472672b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Plausible values"}, {"id": "9fcc7a1f-4b57-4b2b-a1b6-2507882416ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Minimal clinically important difference"}]}]}, {"id": "7c48f7d3-fa5b-441e-8b1e-49655a23a4ae", "type": "topic", "title": "Hypothesis Testing, p-Values, Type I/II Error, and Statistical Power", "description": "Develops responsible test interpretation without reducing evidence to a single p-value.", "children": [{"id": "66f8a803-57d1-4764-b701-4eb6394f51ac", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Testing Framework", "description": "Students learn the logic behind formal statistical tests.", "children": [{"id": "c8c8fe7d-5f2e-4ed9-858b-273686f8b0f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Null hypothesis"}, {"id": "c15331c8-86b5-490d-9309-db5c6b705231", "type": "concept", "title": "Alternative hypothesis"}, {"id": "6db32217-849d-43db-8ef2-1b1d7f98a041", "type": "concept", "title": "Test statistic"}, {"id": "2955c59c-8721-4f9c-a493-57c86256101a", "type": "concept", "title": "p-value"}, {"id": "d52e02d5-8db6-49ff-890f-4588637abf7a", "type": "concept", "title": "Significance level"}]}, {"id": "553efbc4-b1a3-4b29-b31e-0c82751ebc64", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Errors and Power", "description": "This subtopic explains why studies can be wrong or underpowered.", "children": [{"id": "97d32f2b-842a-40f8-a7e6-f6e35b3b4a52", "type": "concept", "title": "Type I error"}, {"id": "361b1f0f-3eb2-4740-9df6-40afa85c6f47", "type": "concept", "title": "Type II error"}, {"id": "74c9e4aa-bd75-41f5-aa5a-845f00681ff8", "type": "concept", "title": "Power"}, {"id": "b0eac7b6-791e-450f-855b-6117760bfbdc", "type": "concept", "title": "Sample size"}, {"id": "451f6ecf-fd30-4d18-a1cf-f832ca458d81", "type": "concept", "title": "Effect size"}]}, {"id": "cfd0e099-9b6a-4afa-bbbd-822e746ebded", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interpreting p-Values Responsibly", "description": "Students avoid common misreadings of statistical significance.", "children": [{"id": "1248af00-87d6-480d-84dd-b1ef8e9dd469", "type": "concept", "title": "Not probability the null is true"}, {"id": "94992be7-3df6-4c2d-8423-2414f6f28576", "type": "concept", "title": "Not effect size"}, {"id": "d9b4e67e-98a5-4096-ba13-1f60f2ed1a0d", "type": "concept", "title": "Multiple testing"}, {"id": "e960c8fb-de19-46a2-a561-e3c596e0533d", "type": "concept", "title": "Borderline p-values"}, {"id": "4d1c354a-b7e1-46b6-8e80-2510fd093976", "type": "concept", "title": "Pre-specified analysis"}]}]}, {"id": "0b4f821a-9b89-4d33-b4a6-fccca83018be", "type": "topic", "title": "Comparing Two Groups: z-Tests, t-Tests, Paired Designs, and Effect Sizes", "description": "Covers common comparisons for means, proportions, paired data, and clinically meaningful differences.", "children": [{"id": "01139cfe-5b03-49ac-b488-072f8a68c280", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparing Means", "description": "Students learn methods for continuous outcomes in two groups.", "children": [{"id": "8c9cbf81-ca73-4792-b3ef-8af33949b9ad", "type": "concept", "title": "One-sample t-test"}, {"id": "8dd8ba89-88aa-4cfe-bc09-5a1517f2d9b6", "type": "concept", "title": "Independent samples t-test"}, {"id": "34053d85-d81a-4158-97ac-798983d8e75d", "type": "concept", "title": "Paired t-test"}, {"id": "70ae1e6e-b967-4dff-8eb6-a6c39eab7312", "type": "concept", "title": "Welch t-test"}, {"id": "eb851313-31c2-43ba-8454-ebb474805657", "type": "concept", "title": "Mean difference"}]}, {"id": "0efed256-96b2-4dc6-b340-5e8cf207f5a8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparing Proportions", "description": "This subtopic covers binary outcomes such as infection, readmission, or screening positivity.", "children": [{"id": "a18b2875-314d-490c-b9e5-f5d103e304c2", "type": "concept", "title": "One-proportion test"}, {"id": "39348340-b4ac-4607-92be-0eee7d2901de", "type": "concept", "title": "Two-proportion test"}, {"id": "6bc54ebb-fd72-47ab-87c5-33f6d9f64e53", "type": "concept", "title": "z-test"}, {"id": "d141223f-3667-4245-902e-7a30ba6f6f5b", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk difference"}, {"id": "a9266bc2-f7db-4c05-8f57-7dd771a6dace", "type": "concept", "title": "Number needed to treat"}]}, {"id": "82ce25a4-6ba8-4682-a232-021fd428390c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Effect Size and Assumptions", "description": "Students report magnitude and check conditions, not just p-values.", "children": [{"id": "6a42adad-59f9-4046-8940-6c9b2c98a62d", "type": "concept", "title": "Cohen's d"}, {"id": "d85a4b8e-99e9-4149-aa6e-d0514bcfd0f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Normality"}, {"id": "b66ee7f4-c8f3-49f4-880e-39f31f0418cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Equal variance"}, {"id": "200fbc92-43da-4494-83db-cafec9f5cc04", "type": "concept", "title": "Independence"}, {"id": "f044c2ba-f5ae-4b47-b9ac-c39f934ca21a", "type": "concept", "title": "Outlier sensitivity"}]}]}, {"id": "7050e6c6-eb33-4cdf-8b18-bde8bb063e7e", "type": "topic", "title": "Comparing Multiple Groups: ANOVA, Post Hoc Tests, and Repeated Measures", "description": "Extends group comparison to multi-arm clinical and health-science settings.", "children": [{"id": "91c1705b-12f0-433a-bd27-14362fa96acb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "One-Way ANOVA", "description": "Students compare more than two group means in health settings.", "children": [{"id": "18661e45-eb73-4b25-ae78-880f71b4c127", "type": "concept", "title": "Between-group variation"}, {"id": "d8665da0-1511-471b-bb37-4460aa738d35", "type": "concept", "title": "Within-group variation"}, {"id": "390bc01b-c458-4979-8a02-859ccc82966f", "type": "concept", "title": "F statistic"}, {"id": "271d02bc-542c-484d-be0e-8fad4fba79cc", "type": "concept", "title": "ANOVA table"}, {"id": "95a8847d-e718-4dbd-bf94-44ac59eef1ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Omnibus test"}]}, {"id": "c634474b-382e-43bf-bd34-19bec55c1a55", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Post Hoc and Planned Comparisons", "description": "This subtopic handles which groups differ after a global test.", "children": [{"id": "ef61f24d-5b66-426d-b32e-9d375472174d", "type": "concept", "title": "Tukey test"}, {"id": "79ee9872-e444-4388-89f9-9d7e3dcc0862", "type": "concept", "title": "Bonferroni adjustment"}, {"id": "7758d062-2af6-4761-81c7-43b0a9e16e44", "type": "concept", "title": "Planned contrast"}, {"id": "9d60f55f-b4c0-4d03-bc53-03157adaeaed", "type": "concept", "title": "Multiple comparisons"}, {"id": "f21c99c1-e079-4027-9b66-fa9ecea8dd12", "type": "concept", "title": "Familywise error"}]}, {"id": "e9296ec2-5c25-4862-808f-69a865069049", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Repeated Measures Concepts", "description": "Students recognize paired or longitudinal designs that violate independence.", "children": [{"id": "1e957853-1711-4e41-9271-658c460900c9", "type": "concept", "title": "Repeated measures"}, {"id": "9583ac6b-0e19-4272-b3d1-7302313db397", "type": "concept", "title": "Within-subject design"}, {"id": "2969241a-449c-4a20-8664-b037a95566f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Baseline and follow-up"}, {"id": "c1a5dc2b-2a88-4cd2-8d5a-83ae7fb2035b", "type": "concept", "title": "Sphericity"}, {"id": "2c812c31-3c4c-4652-a8f5-bd95195f4b95", "type": "concept", "title": "Mixed model preview"}]}]}, {"id": "7732ab4b-4446-469a-a619-b68a881476f1", "type": "topic", "title": "Categorical Data: Chi-Square, Fisher Exact, Risk Ratios, Odds Ratios, and Screening Metrics", "description": "Focuses on binary and categorical outcomes common in clinical, public-health, and nursing research.", "children": [{"id": "7051d9dd-58e6-4386-9e54-be6e53d38239", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Chi-Square Methods", "description": "Students analyze relationships between categorical variables.", "children": [{"id": "36898550-88f8-48d3-a57e-50441e39ba3c", "type": "concept", "title": "Chi-square test of independence"}, {"id": "305d20a6-21ab-4084-987a-65ade52df7e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Goodness-of-fit"}, {"id": "2eba0475-378a-4dfb-a24b-4783a777ffec", "type": "concept", "title": "Expected counts"}, {"id": "dc918c04-10bb-457a-ab08-a12a0ac37662", "type": "concept", "title": "Degrees of freedom"}, {"id": "a1c75983-f653-46ec-bbb6-9200a279fe42", "type": "concept", "title": "Standardized residuals"}]}, {"id": "2703633c-e852-45ac-94c3-3f2c61c09711", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Small Samples and Exact Tests", "description": "This subtopic covers methods when expected counts are too small.", "children": [{"id": "caa0c759-1e00-487d-83a0-b979b25b2935", "type": "concept", "title": "Fisher exact test"}, {"id": "adb79f44-08e8-4ff0-9e51-9ce664a2e48c", "type": "concept", "title": "2x2 table"}, {"id": "d9cb37a0-fa7e-4618-beba-e923ae97cd03", "type": "concept", "title": "Continuity correction"}, {"id": "49b5a001-163d-43e8-b6dd-8fa62124b8d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Sparse cells"}, {"id": "281aef11-b28a-4afe-bb7b-257044955cfd", "type": "concept", "title": "Exact p-value"}]}, {"id": "151b7543-b61e-4670-9a1e-9dea1bf2f5a7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Association and Screening Measures", "description": "Students interpret effect measures common in epidemiology and clinical research.", "children": [{"id": "b760c9eb-878a-4cf9-88f7-8c2ed118458e", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk ratio"}, {"id": "ba745424-9b16-44a9-8863-09b8a791c946", "type": "concept", "title": "Odds ratio"}, {"id": "53e047b3-92ec-49d2-ae3b-de7786283544", "type": "concept", "title": "Relative risk reduction"}, {"id": "188635f7-79b3-47ce-9b45-859308c9ec83", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensitivity"}, {"id": "290bec54-91f4-436a-a717-12e65c9fc970", "type": "concept", "title": "Specificity"}]}]}, {"id": "07d1a8d7-22e2-4f7b-9bfb-d5779e2af038", "type": "topic", "title": "Nonparametric and Robust Methods for Skewed or Ordinal Health Data", "description": "Gives alternatives when assumptions are not met or data are ordinal, skewed, or small-sample.", "children": [{"id": "950edac9-81cd-41eb-85f3-7792e0f402d6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "When Nonparametric Tests Help", "description": "Students identify when rank-based methods are more appropriate.", "children": [{"id": "5700c95f-78ac-4130-b02f-c5b1445a5601", "type": "concept", "title": "Ordinal data"}, {"id": "cee3ea71-b0ef-41bb-bef5-a34eaf982523", "type": "concept", "title": "Skewed data"}, {"id": "97bdef48-afaa-4e78-b8b8-8963d7e4fd85", "type": "concept", "title": "Small samples"}, {"id": "700994b7-42a5-4c8f-83e8-357f9b4fe4fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Outliers"}, {"id": "d3eb73f3-9881-44b9-8ecd-4f42966bfb4d", "type": "concept", "title": "Assumption violations"}]}, {"id": "7f23ac84-7266-43f0-be4c-5249bd0d2f9d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rank-Based Tests", "description": "This subtopic covers common alternatives to t-tests and ANOVA.", "children": [{"id": "3f86473a-32ab-4837-af49-71e1dfc6bad7", "type": "concept", "title": "Mann-Whitney U"}, {"id": "ebb410fa-1dd0-45ce-9fa6-bb24bf5ff554", "type": "concept", "title": "Wilcoxon signed-rank"}, {"id": "ac71c658-06e4-4a0e-bf30-1f0d141ec65b", "type": "concept", "title": "Kruskal-Wallis"}, {"id": "63c80606-7947-4081-9a9c-cf726eb5c02e", "type": "concept", "title": "Friedman test"}, {"id": "97bbbe09-8d9a-4633-b388-3883fd0c7068", "type": "concept", "title": "Median comparison"}]}, {"id": "788c3935-adfa-45c4-a83a-1a5967c3fb37", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Robust Reporting", "description": "Students learn summaries and interpretations that fit non-normal health data.", "children": [{"id": "d9e131cd-76eb-4197-8497-30eceaac09fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Median and IQR"}, {"id": "635dbf76-29fa-4012-9de5-b2408409556e", "type": "concept", "title": "Boxplot"}, {"id": "63b7f3e2-9e21-4e55-b8c5-e715e7ed6975", "type": "concept", "title": "Rank"}, {"id": "b1a97942-d1a8-490b-a1bf-bb14a23e3ca5", "type": "concept", "title": "Robustness"}, {"id": "4b9d686f-2f65-4756-adf9-4ac6ce7cbe0f", "type": "concept", "title": "Distribution-free inference"}]}]}, {"id": "fe01bfcd-1284-4e4d-b15b-4974a764f2fa", "type": "topic", "title": "Correlation, Simple Linear Regression, and Model Interpretation", "description": "Introduces association and prediction for continuous outcomes in health research.", "children": [{"id": "64bda970-4c00-49bb-a562-b55d65d4652b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Correlation", "description": "Students quantify association between two continuous variables.", "children": [{"id": "e45f4f24-c62b-4c95-b553-be545823c943", "type": "concept", "title": "Pearson correlation"}, {"id": "10529075-7bef-40a2-9fc3-ceb7294ba10a", "type": "concept", "title": "Spearman correlation"}, {"id": "81f0359f-08e2-481d-9a42-a7042a084275", "type": "concept", "title": "Direction"}, {"id": "763e87d1-f801-439f-9d09-e2a39528621a", "type": "concept", "title": "Strength"}, {"id": "ab551365-00f5-4349-bebd-9491a9d23815", "type": "concept", "title": "Correlation is not causation"}]}, {"id": "80918a07-073e-4b5f-b807-68568c1dc451", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Simple Linear Regression", "description": "This subtopic introduces prediction and relationship modeling.", "children": [{"id": "d47d4411-eb3c-407e-af18-c09befcff402", "type": "concept", "title": "Outcome variable"}, {"id": "213d6775-0b98-45e4-a2c9-9e1045bd1934", "type": "concept", "title": "Predictor variable"}, {"id": "68bf4185-ee40-40a5-8d21-4f1e2ccffe5b", "type": "concept", "title": "Slope"}, {"id": "7211e06c-8d52-49c3-a2f3-fdcaf0b0ee3d", "type": "concept", "title": "Intercept"}, {"id": "4a44